  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leveraging the Humanitarian-Development Nexus for Ukraine Response through Diaspora Engagement in Italy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 24 February, over four million people have fled Ukraine, including 211,038 third country nationals. This situation requires to urgently reflect on possible responses in neighboring countries and beyond, including in Italy, adopting a rights-based approach, with a view to link humanitarian assistance, peace and long-term development. This project&apos;s purpose is to promote the humanitarian-development nexus approach by fostering a conductive environment for Ukrainian diasporas&apos; active role in response to current crisis. The specific objective is to facilitate dialogue between Ukrainian diaspora organizations and national and local stakeholders in Italy, and Ukrainian diaspora response.</narrative>
  </description>
